cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Anu Architecture: standardized 8-phase econometric project scaffold"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anderson
    given-names: Nicholas
    email: nickawebbox@gmail.com
    affiliation: "The New School for Social Research"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # Nick to fill
repository-code: "https://github.com/andenick/anu-architecture"
abstract: >-
  A standardized 8-phase architecture (Setup, Load, Process, Validate, Manual,
  Analyze, Output, Explore) for econometric data construction and analysis. It
  scaffolds a self-contained, language-agnostic project in which every script,
  dataset, output, and decision is tracked in one folder, under containment,
  no-synthetic-data, justified-proxy, reproducibility-without-agents, and
  audit-trail principles. It is a standalone member skill of the Anu Framework.
keywords:
  - econometrics
  - data-pipeline
  - reproducible-research
  - python
